\name{CandlestickPatterns}
\alias{CandlestickPatterns}
\title{Candlestick pattern recognisers an instrument runs over its candles}
\description{
TA-Lib's recognisers for named one to five candle formations. Each method fetches the instrument's candles through \code{prices()}, adds one column and returns the candles. The class is a link in the chain of analysis classes that \code{Instrument} inherits, and \code{Instrument} supplies \code{prices()}.

The recognisers come from the \code{talib} package, which wraps the same TA-Lib C library as Python's \code{talib}. Its signals are read as 100 and -100, not 1 and -1, and the candles at the start that TA-Lib cannot judge get 0, as in Python.
}
